====================================================================================================================
  DOES THE ULTIMATE INVESTOR IV-RANK FILTER MAKE DELTA-10 SHORT OPTIONS MORE CONSISTENT?
  Real causal VIX + SPY (same series as scripts/test_vol_risk_premium.py / run_vol_risk_premium.py).
  This is a FILTER-LOGIC validation, NOT a full profitability verdict (that is sec 20, already KILLED).
====================================================================================================================

  Data: 1993-01-29 -> 2026-06-16  (8,402 trading days)
  IV-rank warm-up: first eligible date for EITHER group = 1994-01-26 (needs 252 trading days of trailing VIX)
  Filtered (top-tercile IV rank) days: 2,796 / 8,151 eligible days (34.3%)

####################################################################################################################
  *** TAIL RISK -- READ THIS FIRST *** (pooled put+call book per group, real subsequent SPY/VIX path)
####################################################################################################################

  FILTERED (IV rank top-tercile)
    worst single day:   -69.5%  on 2020-03-16 00:00:00
    worst single month: -91.0%  on 2008-10
    worst single TRADE (return on premium collected): -4034%  (put worst -4034%, call worst -126%)
    trades losing >100% of premium collected: 12/362
    KILL ON TAIL RISK (bar: day<-30% or month<-50%): YES

  UNFILTERED (control, no IV condition)
    worst single day:   -74.9%  on 2008-10-15 00:00:00
    worst single month: -93.3%  on 2008-10
    worst single TRADE (return on premium collected): -12675%  (put worst -12675%, call worst -225%)
    trades losing >100% of premium collected: 15/616
    KILL ON TAIL RISK (bar: day<-30% or month<-50%): YES

