    FILTERED (IV rank top-tercile)           Sharpe +0.38 -> DSR 0.287 (n_obs=4760)
    UNFILTERED (control, no IV condition)    Sharpe +0.53 -> DSR 0.545 (n_obs=8141)

####################################################################################################################
  PER-YEAR CONCENTRATION
####################################################################################################################
  FILTERED (IV rank top-tercile): top-year share of total log-return = 23%
  UNFILTERED (control, no IV condition): top-year share of total log-return = 18%

####################################################################################################################
  LOOK-AHEAD GUARD
####################################################################################################################
  FILTERED-group entries re-derived from raw VIX (never trusting the precomputed series): 362 checked, using only data through each entry's PRIOR trading day (one full day of delay, same shift(1) convention as sec 20).
  UNFILTERED-group entries: 616 (no IV condition to violate by construction).
  PASS -- every FILTERED entry's eligibility independently re-verified from raw VIX using only information available strictly before that entry was opened.

====================================================================================================================
  VERDICT
====================================================================================================================
  win rate:      filtered 97%  vs  unfiltered 97%  -> filter does NOT improve win rate
  outcome sd:    filtered 248.0%  vs  unfiltered 535.4%  -> filter REDUCES variance of outcomes
  worst day:     filtered -69.5%  vs  unfiltered -74.9%
  worst month:   filtered -91.0%  vs  unfiltered -93.3%  -> filter REDUCES tail risk on this specific metric
  BOTH groups breach the sec-20 catastrophic single-day/-month bar. The IV filter does NOT remove the
  underlying naked-short-option tail risk -- it can only change how OFTEN you are exposed to it.

  PLAIN ANSWER: does the IV/VIX filter meaningfully improve consistency vs no filter? NO / MIXED
  This is a filter-logic validation only -- it says nothing about whether either group is profitable
  enough to trade once compared to buy-and-hold (that comparison is out of scope here; see sec 20 for
  the full-strategy verdict on naked short vol, which was KILL regardless of any filter).

  NEW TRIALS: 2 (filtered cell, unfiltered cell; each pools its put-book + call-book).
  Cumulative project trials after this batch: 1087 (1085 prior + 2).
  saved -> results/delta10_iv_filter.csv, results/delta10_iv_filter_trades.csv, results/delta10_iv_filter_run.log
